Subject: dostor: do not publish aborted uploads when -0 (--notruncate) is set

With -0, pure-ftpd uploads into a hidden .pureftpd-upload.* temp and renames
it onto the requested name. dostor() performs that rename before it looks at
the transfer result, so a transfer that ended in "451 Transfer aborted"
(client TCP reset, idle timeout, ABOR, dropped control connection) is
published under its final name exactly like a completed one. Cameras on a
flaky Wi-Fi link therefore leave truncated DSC01833.ARW files behind on every
failed attempt, and retry the same name until one completes.

Skip the rename when the transfer failed and this was not a REST resume; the
existing cleanup at the end: label then unlinks the temp. Resumes keep the
stock behaviour since the temp holds the client's pre-existing bytes.

Applies to upstream 1.0.50 and current master (the block is unchanged).

--- a/src/ftpd.c
+++ b/src/ftpd.c
@@ -4353,6 +4353,15 @@
                 atomic_file = NULL;
             }
         } else if (atomic_file != NULL) {
+            /* FTP-Camera-Dropbox: never publish an aborted upload. When the
+             * transfer ended with an error (peer reset, idle timeout, ABOR,
+             * dropped control connection) skip the rename; the cleanup at
+             * end: unlinks the .pureftpd-upload.* temp instead. Resumed
+             * uploads (restartat > 0) keep the stock behaviour because the
+             * temp then holds the client's pre-existing bytes. */
+            if (ret != 0 && restartat == (off_t) 0) {
+                goto afterquota;
+            }
             if ((atomic_file_size = get_file_size(atomic_file)) < (off_t) 0) {
                 goto afterquota;
             }
